    "explanation": "$M_r(\\ce{KMnO4}) = 39 + 55 + 64 = 158$, so $1.58 \\div 158 = 0.0100$ mol. The ratio $\\ce{KMnO4} : \\ce{O2} = 2 : 1$ gives $0.00500$ mol of $\\ce{O2}$, which is $0.00500 \\times 24\\,000 = 120\\ \\text{cm}^3$: more than the syringe holds. For 100 cm³: $n(\\ce{O2}) = 100 \\div 24\\,000 = 0.004167$ mol, so $n(\\ce{KMnO4}) = 0.008333$ mol and mass $= 0.008333 \\times 158 = 1.32$ g.\n\n*Syllabus note: Cambridge IGCSE Supplement (Extended) content.*",
